<p>
  Two losses train TDV jointly. The <strong>MSE loss</strong> directly supervises the causal constraint — the predicted next-frame embedding must match the teacher's encoding of the actual next frame. The <strong>DINO-style cross-entropy loss</strong> applied over projection heads prevents collapse — if all frames mapped to the same embedding, the prototype distributions would be identical and the CE loss would spike. The two losses are combined as L = λ<sub>mse</sub>·L<sub>mse</sub> + λ<sub>dino</sub>·L<sub>dino</sub>.
</p>
